WEBVTT

00:00:09,170 --> 00:00:17,170
I've used my new RIF3 nights. Tonight, the Sunday program started beeping, almost like a truck going backwards.

00:00:17,170 --> 00:00:29,170
Since this makes sleep impossible, I ran the Saturday program again. Notice a high pitch, but low volume noise from the RIF as well. Is this normal? What do I do about the beeping?

00:00:29,170 --> 00:00:35,170
Unfortunately, that is normal. It will beep more at different frequencies.

00:00:35,170 --> 00:00:55,170
And there's nothing that you could do about the beeping. Now, you can use the amplifier, jackhammer with it and keep the bulb under the bed and cover the RIF machine up. That will help.

00:00:55,170 --> 00:01:03,170
Most people will just get used to it and then they just sleep through it and it doesn't cause a problem.

00:01:03,170 --> 00:01:15,170
We've had some people that had had to go to the point to put it ear plugs in. But now, with the jackhammer, you shouldn't have to do that. You can cover it up and you'll still get the benefits from it.

